    "prompt_prefix": "",
    "prompt_suffix": "Style: candid documentary photograph of a real place, not an advertisement, not CGI, not a composite. Shot on a full-frame camera with a 35mm lens at about f/2.8, standing eye level, available light only, true-to-life restrained colour, mild sensor noise, a slight handheld tilt, honest texture on skin, concrete, paper, painted steel and glass. Printed sheets and painted labels may clip a little but the overall image stays natural — never glowing, never hyper-saturated, no HDR look, no rim-light effects, no lens flare. NUMBER RULE: every Korean amount quoted in this prompt is printed on ONE unbroken line, never split in the middle of a digit group, and every character of the largest quoted line is at least one twelfth of the frame height so it still reads when the picture is shrunk to thumbnail size. LETTERING RULE: render only the Korean words and figures quoted in this prompt; every other sheet, notice, wall, board and sign in the frame is blank paper or printed too small and slightly out of focus to read — do not invent english text, latin letters, chinese characters, gibberish text, random lettering or invented words anywhere in the image. No title overlay text, no captions, no subtitle bars, no large lettering across the frame, no watermark, no graphic arrows, no highlight circles, no drawn charts and no overlaid panels."
