    {
      "id": 1,
      "purpose": "content",
      "composition": "좌우 대비",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「같은 계단인데 한 칸 위는 내 돈으로 못 올라간다」. 40대 중앙값 2억 8,384만 원과 50대 중앙값 3억 1,685만 원을 아래·위 층계참 벽에 각각 붙여, 나이 한 칸의 차이를 실물 단차로 보여준다(verified-data 1절). [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 월급쟁이 남성) — 특수직업·다른세대·성공자 아님 [B 금액] \"2억 8,384만 원\" / \"3억 1,685만 원\" [C 사건] 발을 다음 단에 올리는 중, 손끝은 아직 종이에 닿아 있음 [D 주어] 내 나이 칸 숫자를 확인하다 다음 칸 높이에 걸린 사람이 나다 [구도] 좌우대비 [텍스트] 제목「8층, 당신 자리는 몇 층입니까」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까」 — 층 개수가 아니라 멈추는 지점을 말한다",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the shadowed concrete landing and the dark out-of-focus shoulder of the man nearest the camera, so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand, no sheet of paper and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — every face, hand, painted label and taped sheet sits in the upper five-eighths, and both landings run across the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the man in the navy work jacket is the largest thing in the picture — his head and shoulders occupy the entire left third of the frame, his face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of his hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and his shoulder leaves the frame on the left. The woman on the upper landing is far smaller, roughly one third of his head height. SCENE: the interior stairwell of an old Korean commercial building, photographed straight on from the lower landing at standing eye level. One thick concrete riser cuts the frame vertically down the middle — the left half is the lower landing, the right half is the next landing a full body height above it, its edge chipped and repainted many times over. On the left wall, stencilled in white paint, a label reads \"40대\" in Korean Hangul, and an A4 sheet taped under it reads \"2억 8,384만 원\" in heavy black print across the full width of the page. On the right wall, higher up, the same white stencil reads \"50대\" in Korean Hangul with a taped sheet under it reading \"3억 1,685만 원\". Lived-in clutter fills the shaft — layered old tape marks, a red fire extinguisher, wiring stapled along the wall, a mop leaning in the corner, scuffed grey treads. Warm late-afternoon light falls through a small dusty stairwell window on the right while a cold fluorescent tube burns overhead, the two light sources mixing on the faces. PEOPLE: the man in his forties is caught mid-step, his right foot already lifted onto the riser and his left fingertips still pressed flat against the taped sheet — eyes wide open showing whites, mouth open, eyebrows pushed high, a bead of sweat at his temple. The woman in her fifties stands on the upper landing in a beige cardigan with her arms folded, lips pressed tight, chin lowered, looking down at him without moving."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "purpose": "content",
      "composition": "현장 + 군중 반응",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「같은 계단길에서 사람마다 멈춘 칸이 다르다」. 30대 중앙값 1억 5,585만 원을 담벼락 벽보로 세워, 나이 칸마다 멈추는 높이가 갈린다는 본문 뼈대를 현장으로 보여준다(verified-data 1절). [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 여성, 장바구니 든 동네 주민) [B 금액] \"1억 5,585만 원\" [C 사건] 계단을 오르다 멈춰 접힌 종이를 펴는 중, 뒷사람들은 아직 올라오는 중 [D 주어] 내가 지금 몇 번째 칸에 서 있는지가 화면의 주제다 [구도] 현장군중 [텍스트] 제목「연령별 순자산 8층」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty ground. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the dark backs and shoulders of the two people nearest the camera on the lowest steps, so far out of focus and so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand, no notice and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — every face, hand, painted riser and wall notice sits in the upper five-eighths, and the painted risers begin at the MIDDLE of the frame and climb upward from there, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the woman in the quilted jacket is the largest thing in the picture — her head and shoulders occupy the entire right third of the frame, her face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of her hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and her shoulder leaves the frame on the right. The other climbers are far smaller, roughly one third of her head height. SCENE: a long outdoor concrete staircase running up a steep old Korean hillside neighbourhood, photographed from the foot of the flight at standing eye level, looking straight up the climb. Four or five ordinary people in their thirties to fifties have stopped at different heights, spread out up the steps. White paint is stencilled across three of the risers, reading \"30대\", \"40대\" and \"50대\" in Korean Hangul from the lower steps upward. On the red-brick retaining wall beside the flight a large printed notice, as wide as the wall panel behind it, reads \"1억 5,585만 원\" in heavy black characters. Honest lived-in detail everywhere — cracked cement patches, a rusted water pipe, potted plants in styrofoam boxes, a bicycle chained to a post, laundry poles on a low roof, a stack of blank flyers curling under a stone. Soft late-afternoon light comes over the top of the hill. PEOPLE: the woman in her forties has stopped mid-climb with one foot still on the higher step, opening a folded A4 sheet whose crease is still standing up, her head just lifted from it — eyebrows raised, mouth slightly open, one hand gripping the paper edge. Behind and below her two men keep climbing with their heads down, one carrying a shopping bag, neither of them looking at her."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "purpose": "content",
      "composition": "인물 감정 클로즈업",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「내 나이의 꼭대기 값이 이 숫자다」. 50대 상위 1% 커트라인 34억 5,000만 원(verified-data 2절)을 손에 든 종이로 얼굴 옆에 세워, 같은 상위 1%도 나이마다 값이 다르다는 이 편의 핵심 대비를 한 장으로 만든다. [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(50대 직장인 남성) — 은퇴 이후·연금 수급자 아님 [B 금액] \"34억 5,000만 원\" [C 사건] 종이를 방금 펴는 중, 다른 손이 아직 접힌 자국을 누르고 있음 [D 주어] 내 나이 칸의 꼭대기를 내가 직접 확인하는 중 [구도] 인물클로즈업 [텍스트] 제목「당신 자리는 몇 층입니까」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the man's dark shoulder and the shadowed concrete landing behind him, so deeply in shadow and so far out of focus that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand and no sheet of paper sits in that bottom three-eighths — his face, both his hands and the sheet all sit in the upper five-eighths, and the sheet is held at the MIDDLE height of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the man in his fifties is the largest thing in the picture — his head and shoulders occupy the entire right third of the frame, his face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of his hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and his shoulder leaves the frame on the right. SCENE: a stairwell landing in an old Korean office building, photographed straight on at standing eye level. The man has just unfolded an A4 sheet and holds it up beside his own face, tilted flat toward the lens so that it fills the left third of the frame at mid height, while his other hand still presses the fold down. Thick handwritten marker on that sheet reads \"34억 5,000만 원\" in Korean Hangul right across the width of the page, with a much smaller line above it reading \"50대 상위 1%\". Around him the stairwell is worn and honest — a corkboard with blank curling sheets pinned to it, a dented steel fire door, wiring stapled along the wall, a paper cup left on the window ledge, a scuffed grey floor. Warm late-afternoon light comes through the dusty stairwell window behind him and a cold fluorescent tube burns above, the two lights mixing across his face. PEOPLE: his eyes are wide open showing whites, his jaw hangs slack, his eyebrows are pushed high and pulled together, and a bead of sweat sits at his temple; he is staring at the sheet, not at the camera, and his shoulders have gone stiff."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "purpose": "title",
      "composition": "현장 + 군중 반응",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「층마다 붙은 금액이 이렇게 벌어져 있다」. 확정 제목의 「8층」을 실물 층별 안내판으로 이행한다 — 8층 47억 4,000만 원(상위 0.5%)과 4층 10억 원(10억 이상 11.8%)을 같은 판에 세운다(verified-data 2절). [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 남성, 분양상담센터에 들른 방문객) [B 금액] \"47억 4,000만 원\" / \"10억 원\" [C 사건] 손가락이 4층 줄에 막 닿는 중 [D 주어] 내가 닿을 수 있는 칸이 어디까지인지를 직접 짚는다 [구도] 현장군중 [텍스트] 제목「대한민국 순자산 8층」 vs 썸네일「연령별 순자산 8층 표 / 내 자리는?」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the dark backs and shoulders of the visitors nearest the camera, so far out of focus and so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand, no board and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — every face, hand and printed row sits in the upper five-eighths, and the information board and the counter run across the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the man in his forties is the largest thing in the picture — his head and shoulders occupy the entire right third of the frame, his face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of his hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and his shoulder leaves the frame on the right. The other visitors are far smaller, roughly one third of his head height. SCENE: the lobby of a Korean apartment sales and model-house centre, photographed straight on at standing eye level. A large matte information board is mounted flat on the wall and fills more than half the frame width at mid height, its surface ruled into rows for each floor. The top row reads \"8층\" in Korean Hangul with \"47억 4,000만 원\" printed beside it in tall black characters, and a row near the middle of the board reads \"4층\" with \"10억 원\" beside it; every other row on the board is printed too small and slightly out of focus to read. Ordinary venue clutter fills the rest of the room — a paper cup stack beside a water dispenser, a scale model of a housing block under a scratched acrylic cover, folding chairs, a floor fan, a roll of masking tape and blank leaflets on the counter. Daylight comes through the wide front glass and mixes with warm ceiling downlights. PEOPLE: the man has just raised his arm and his index finger is touching the \"4층\" row, his other hand still holding a rolled leaflet — eyes narrowed hard, lips parted, eyebrows drawn down. Two visitors behind him are much smaller, both craning up at the top row, one with a hand covering her mouth."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "purpose": "title",
      "composition": "화면 클로즈업",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「내 나이 칸의 꼭대기는 손가락 한 줄 위에 있다」. 40대 상위 1% 커트라인 32억 원(verified-data 2절)을 식탁에 펼친 표의 한 줄로 만들어, 같은 40대 안에서 중앙값과 꼭대기가 자릿수로 갈린다는 본문을 지목한다. [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 여성, 집에서 표를 확인하는 주부·직장인) [B 금액] \"32억 원\" [C 사건] 손끝이 한 줄을 따라 미끄러지는 중, 다른 손이 종이 모서리를 눌러 펴는 중 [D 주어] 식탁 위 그 줄이 내 나이 칸이다 [구도] 화면클로즈업 [텍스트] 제목「내 자리는 어디쯤」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty table. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the woman's dark forearm and the shadowed near edge of the table top, so far out of focus and so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no printed row and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — her face, her pointing hand and the printed sheet all sit in the upper five-eighths, and the table top runs across the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the woman in her forties is the largest thing in the picture — her head and shoulders occupy the entire right third of the frame, her face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of her hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and her shoulder leaves the frame on the right. SCENE: the kitchen table of an ordinary Korean flat, photographed from slightly above and to the side at seated eye level, the woman leaning in over the table from the right. An A4 printout ruled into rows lies open on the table top at mid height, filling the left half of the frame; the row her fingertip is sliding along reads \"32억 원\" in heavy black print right across the width of the sheet, with a short label at the head of that row reading \"40대\" in Korean Hangul, while every other row on the sheet is printed too small and slightly out of focus to read. Around the sheet sits the honest clutter of a real kitchen — reading glasses folded on the cloth, a ballpoint pen, a half-drunk mug of coffee gone cold, a pill packet, a wall calendar, a laundry rack half seen in the doorway. Flat soft daylight comes from the window on the left and a cool kitchen fluorescent burns overhead. PEOPLE: her fingertip is still moving along the row and her other hand presses the curling corner of the paper flat; her eyes are wide, her mouth is slightly open, her eyebrows are lifted and her head has just tilted back a little, as if she has read the row twice."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "purpose": "title",
      "composition": "좌우 대비",
      "concept_ko": "한 줄 메시지: 「층 하나 위가 사람 키만큼 높다」. 5층 11억 원(상위 10%)과 7층 34억 8,000만 원(상위 1%)을 아래·위 층계참 벽에 각각 세워, 확정 제목의 「8층」 틀에서 위층 간격이 자릿수로 벌어진다는 본문을 이행한다(verified-data 2절). [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 부부) — 성공자·전문가 아님 [B 금액] \"11억 원\" / \"34억 8,000만 원\" [C 사건] 남편이 위쪽을 가리키는 중, 위층 남자는 철문을 밀어 여는 중 [D 주어] 아래 칸에 서서 올려다보는 게 우리 부부다 [구도] 좌우대비 [텍스트] 제목「8층, 당신 자리는 몇 층입니까」 vs 썸네일「나이 칸마다 다른 층 높이 / 어느 층?」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty ground. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the dark backs and shoulders of the couple nearest the camera and the shadowed alley floor, so far out of focus and so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand, no notice and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — every face, hand, stencilled label and taped notice sits in the upper five-eighths, and both landings run across the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the woman in the maroon jacket is the largest thing in the picture — her head and shoulders occupy the entire left third of the frame, her face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of her hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and her shoulder leaves the frame on the left. Her husband beside her is smaller, and the man on the far upper landing is far smaller still, roughly one third of her head height. SCENE: the outdoor concrete staircase bolted to the side of an old Korean low-rise shop building, photographed straight on from the alley at standing eye level. A thick concrete riser splits the frame — a lower landing on the left, a much higher landing on the right, joined by a worn run of steps whose paint has flaked back to bare cement. White stencil paint on the left wall reads \"5층\" in Korean Hangul with a weather-curled notice taped under it reading \"11억 원\" in heavy black print; on the right wall, far higher, the stencil reads \"7층\" with a notice under it reading \"34억 8,000만 원\". Real street detail fills the frame — an air-conditioner condenser bracketed to the wall, coiled hose, stacked plastic crates, a bare bulb over a shop door, tape ghosts where old notices were torn away. It is early evening; warm tungsten light spills out of the shop windows below while the last cold blue of the sky sits above the upper landing. PEOPLE: the couple in their forties stand on the lower landing, the husband's arm just raised to point up at the higher notice, the wife looking up with her eyes wide, mouth open and one hand half lifted toward her collar. On the upper landing a man in his fifties is pushing a steel door open with his back half turned, already stepping through."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "purpose": "reference-inherit",
      "composition": "좌우 대비 — 연령 다단 나열 (앵커 계승)",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 다섯 사람이 한 줄로 나란히 서 있는데 발밑 바닥 높이가 저마다 달라, 같은 줄인데 같은 높이가 아니다 / [남김] 그 한 줄 모순 · 좌에서 우로 한 칸씩 올라가는 층계 단차가 만드는 5분할 경계선 · 다섯 명을 정면으로 담는 서 있는 눈높이 카메라(뒤집지 않음) · 다섯 인물이 상단 5분의 4를 가로로 채우고 각자 발밑에 나이 라벨, 하단은 조용 / [바꿈] 피사체(캐릭터 일러스트 5인 → 실사 한국인 5인, 성별 혼합) · 업종·장소(흰 그라데이션 무배경 → 낡은 상가 계단실) · 관찰 디테일(빨간 상승 곡선 그래픽 → 챌판 흰 스텐실 페인트와 벽에 붙은 커트라인 벽보) ※ 앵커의 5인 전신 나열을 유지해야 하므로 이 장만 얼굴 55~60% 대신 「가운데 40대 남성이 반 발짝 앞, 머리 높이 3분의 1」로 잡는다 — 계승 [남김]4가 우선. [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(가운데 40대 남성이 주인공) [B 금액] \"13억 1,000만 원\" / \"44억 9,000만 원\" [C 사건] 다섯 명 전부 멈춘 게 아니라 각자 다른 동작 중 [D 주어] 이 줄 어딘가에 내 나이 칸이 있다 [구도] 좌우대비(다단 나열) [텍스트] 제목「연령별 순자산 8층」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까 / 내 자리는?」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the shadowed lowest steps and the dark out-of-focus backs of two people standing below the row, so deeply in shadow that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no hand, no notice and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — all five people, every painted riser label and both wall notices sit in the upper five-eighths, and the run of steps crosses the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge. SCALE, INHERITED FROM THE ANCHOR: five people stand in one unbroken row straight across the upper part of the frame, each one standing a single riser higher than the person to their left, so the line of heads climbs steadily from left to right; the man in his forties at the centre of the row is half a step nearer the camera and is the largest figure, his head spanning roughly the top third of the frame height, and the other four are noticeably smaller as the steps rise away from him. SCENE: the inside of a wide old Korean stairwell that steps up from left to right, photographed dead straight on at standing eye level so that all five people are seen frontally in a single line. White paint is stencilled on the five risers under their feet, reading \"29세\", \"30대\", \"40대\", \"50대\" and \"60대\" in Korean Hangul from left to right. On the left wall a large printed notice reads \"13억 1,000만 원\" in heavy black characters, and on the far right wall a second notice of the same size reads \"44억 9,000만 원\". The shaft is worn and real — flaking green wall paint, a red fire extinguisher, wiring stapled along the wall, a corkboard of blank curling sheets, a bucket left on a landing. Cool daylight comes through a tall dusty window on the right and cold fluorescent tubes burn along the ceiling. PEOPLE: none of them are still. On the far left a man in his late twenties grips his backpack strap and lifts a foot onto the next riser, mouth open, eyes wide. Next a woman in her thirties looks down at a folded sheet in her hand, eyebrows pulled together. At the centre the man in his forties has just raised his head toward the higher steps, eyes wide open showing whites and lips parted. Beyond him a woman in her fifties stands with folded arms looking back down the line, lips pressed tight. On the far right a man in his sixties is half turned away, already reaching for the door at the top."
    },
