      "composition": "좌우 대비 — 연령 다단 나열 (앵커 계승 · 허리 위)",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 다섯 사람이 한 줄로 나란히 서 있는데 발밑 바닥 높이가 저마다 달라, 같은 줄인데 같은 높이가 아니다 / [남김] 그 한 줄 모순 · 좌에서 우로 한 칸씩 올라가는 층계 단차가 만드는 5분할 경계선 · 다섯 명을 정면으로 담는 서 있는 눈높이 카메라(뒤집지 않음) · 다섯 인물이 상단을 가로로 채우고 각자 나이 라벨을 달고 있음 / [바꿈] 피사체(7번과 다른 5인, 여성 중심에 작업복·정장 혼합) · 색온도와 광원(7번의 찬 형광등 → 창으로 드는 늦은 오후 황금빛 역광) · 자세(정면 부동 자세 → 각자 다른 방향으로 몸을 튼 동작) ※ 거리감을 허리 위로 좁혀 7번과 다른 화각. [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(가운데 40대 여성) [B 금액] \"2억 5,060만 원\" / \"5억 5,161만 원\" — 30대 평균과 50대 평균(verified-data 1절) [C 사건] 한 사람은 발을 올리는 중, 한 사람은 종이를 넘기는 중 [D 주어] 나이 칸마다 다른 이 평균이 내 집 이야기다 [구도] 좌우대비(다단 나열) [텍스트] 제목「내 자리는 어디쯤」 vs 썸네일「연령별 순자산 8층 표」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the dark waists and hands of the two people nearest the camera and the deeply shadowed step edges in front of them, so far out of focus that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no notice and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — all five faces, both wall notices and every painted label sit in the upper five-eighths. SCALE, INHERITED FROM THE ANCHOR: five people stand in one unbroken row straight across the frame, cropped at the waist, each one standing a single riser higher than the person to their left so that the line of heads climbs steadily from left to right; the woman in her forties at the centre is nearest the camera and is the largest figure, her head spanning roughly forty percent of the frame height, the others smaller as the steps rise away. SCENE: a broad indoor staircase in an old Korean community building that steps up from left to right, photographed dead straight on at standing eye level so all five are seen frontally in one line. Behind them a tall window runs the width of the wall and the low late-afternoon sun pours straight through it, throwing long warm shadows forward and rimming the row in golden light while the wall faces fall into deep shade. White paint is stencilled on the risers under their feet reading \"29세\", \"30대\", \"40대\", \"50대\" and \"60대\" in Korean Hangul from left to right. On the left wall a printed notice reads \"2억 5,060만 원\" in heavy black characters, and on the right wall a matching notice reads \"5억 5,161만 원\". Honest detail fills the rest — a taped-over noticeboard of blank sheets, a folded step ladder, a floor mop, dust hanging in the sun shaft. PEOPLE: every one of them is turned a different way. On the left a young woman in a work vest twists back over her shoulder with her mouth open. Beside her a man in his thirties is turning a page of the sheet in his hands, brow furrowed. At the centre the woman in her forties has stopped square to the camera with her eyes wide open and one hand pressed flat to her chest. Beyond her a man in his fifties is stepping up, one foot already on the next riser, jaw set. On the right a woman in her sixties has turned almost fully away toward the top of the flight."
    },
