      "concept_ko": "[모순] 다섯 사람이 한 줄로 나란히 서 있는데 발밑 바닥 높이가 저마다 달라, 같은 줄인데 같은 높이가 아니다 / [남김] 그 한 줄 모순 · 좌에서 우로 한 칸씩 올라가는 층계 단차가 만드는 5분할 경계선 · 다섯 명을 정면으로 담는 서 있는 눈높이 카메라(뒤집지 않음) · 나이 라벨이 붙은 다섯 자리가 화면 안에 그대로 남음 / [바꿈] 피사체(7·8번과 다른 5인, 앞치마·작업복·정장이 섞인 직업 혼합) · 자세(전신 정렬 → 맨 앞 인물이 가슴 위로 크게 나와 벽 라벨을 손끝으로 짚음) · 관찰 디테일(소지품으로 부를 암시하던 앵커 → 챌판의 벗겨진 페인트와 손때 자국) ※ 얼굴 중심 화각이라 이 장에서 실사형 인물 크기 규칙(얼굴 55~60%)을 그대로 적용한다. [A 얼굴] 나 같은 사람(40대 남성, 앞치마 차림 자영업자) [B 금액] \"4억 8,389만 원\" — 40대 순자산 평균(verified-data 1절) [C 사건] 손끝이 벽의 나이 라벨에 막 닿는 중 [D 주어] 내 나이 칸 평균 앞에 선 사람이 나다 [구도] 좌우대비(다단 나열) [텍스트] 제목「당신 자리는 몇 층입니까」 vs 썸네일「우리 나이대는 몇 층에서 멈춥니까 / 내 자리는?」",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge with a real scene — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block, and never a large expanse of bare empty floor. The bottom three-eighths of the frame height is filled by the man's dark shoulder and apron front and the shadowed step edges behind him, so deeply in shadow and so far out of focus that it reads as one single dark mass with no readable detail, which keeps overlay text legible on top of it. No face, no notice and no bright object sits in that bottom three-eighths — his face, his raised hand, the wall notice and the four people behind him all sit in the upper five-eighths. SCALE, EQUALLY IMPORTANT: the man in his forties is the largest thing in the picture — his head and shoulders occupy the entire right third of the frame, his face alone spans roughly the top 55 to 60 percent of the frame height, the top of his hair touches the upper edge and is very slightly cropped by it, and his shoulder leaves the frame on the right. The four other people standing further up the flight are far smaller, roughly one third of his head height, and their line of heads still climbs steadily from left to right behind him. SCENE: the same wide old Korean stairwell that steps up from left to right, photographed dead straight on at standing eye level, but this time from close in beside the man at the near end of the row. White paint is stencilled on the risers behind him reading \"29세\", \"30대\", \"40대\", \"50대\" and \"60대\" in Korean Hangul from left to right, the paint chipped and greasy with old handprints where people have steadied themselves. On the wall right beside his raised hand a printed notice reads \"4억 8,389만 원\" in heavy black characters across the sheet. The stairwell is honest and used — worn nosings on every tread, a delivery crate parked on a landing, a rolled floor mat, blank flyers stuffed behind a pipe. Warm light from a shop doorway below mixes with cold daylight falling from a window at the top. PEOPLE: the man in his forties wears a market apron over a work shirt, his fingertips just touching the stencilled label on the wall — eyes wide open showing whites, mouth open, eyebrows pushed high, the tendons standing out on his neck. Behind him and far smaller, a woman in a work coat looks down at her hands, a man in a suit stares up the flight, a woman in her fifties has stopped mid-step, and a man in his sixties stands highest with his back half turned."
